    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Joseph Kosuth: \"And in Jasper\nJohns' work – such as his 'Target' and 'Flag' paintings and\nhis ale cans – one has a particularly good example of art\nexisting as analytical proposition.\" (\"Art\nafter Philosophy, part II.\" Studio International, November\n1969, p.161)",
